          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01TZ27otiVCfycqwvnARdSaG",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: How credential-scoping and runtime-path decisions work together as a unified architectural principle for centralizing configuration and security at startup.\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - concept/Credential-Scoping\\n  - concept/Runtime-Paths\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both source pages explicitly describe startup-time centralization as their defining principle; the connection is direct and structural.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2027-04-14\\n---\\n\\nBoth [[credential-scoping]] and [[runtime-paths]] operate under the same architectural\\nprinciple: **all configuration and security decisions are made once, at startup, in a\\nsingle place, before the system\u0027s operational agents run**.\\n\\n[[credential-scoping]] achieves its security boundary by centralizing the decision of\\nwhere the Anthropic API key exists \u2014 not in the Hub\u0027s own process environment, but\\ninjected into each agent\u0027s environment at the moment of spawn. The key is never\\ninherited or scattered; one startup routine decides and executes this scoping.\\n\\n[[runtime-paths]] achieves its maintainability by centralizing the decision of where\\nevery file lives \u2014 wiki root, database, secrets file, agent instructions \u2014 in a single\\npath resolver that reads all configuration sources once at startup, validates them, and\\ndistributes the resolved set downstream. No agent rediscovers locations; they all\\nconsume the pre-resolved set.\\n\\nThe shared principle is that each agent process inherits not ambient system state (raw\\nenvironment variables, working directory assumptions, scattered config files) but a\\n**composed, validated, pre-decided state** prepared by one startup routine. This makes\\nthe system:\\n\\n- **Hermetic**: agents do not have to reason about external state; they work from what\\n  they were given.\\n- **Auditable**: you can see exactly what decision was made by inspecting one place.\\n- **Secure**: sensitive choices (like credential presence) are enforced structurally\\n  rather than relying on downstream agents to respect a convention.\\n- **Testable**: a test can swap the composed state without mutating ambient process\\n  state.\\n\\nAdding a new agent or a new runtime location means extending that single composition\\npoint, not scattered throughout the codebase. Scaling the system means making the\\ncomposition richer, not making it more distributed.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
